# TraitMech environment variables
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values.
# .env is gitignored — DO NOT commit it.
#
# `just` loads .env automatically (`set dotenv-load := true`). Scripts run
# directly with `python scripts/...` do NOT get it, so prefer the `just`
# recipes — otherwise research falls back to whatever is in your shell.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Edison Scientific (formerly FutureHouse) — deep research
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The only credential TraitMech needs. Used by scripts/research_trait.py and
# `just research-trait <provider> <category> <slug>`.
#
# Create a key at https://platform.edisonscientific.com/
#
# Note on provider naming: `--provider falcon` IS the Edison provider —
# "Falcon"/"FutureHouse" is the former brand. deep-research-client resolves the
# falcon provider from EDISON_API_KEY (see its client.py), so one key covers it.
EDISON_API_KEY=

# OpenScientist through deep-research-client. Use name:secret, not a bare token.
# OPENSCIENTIST_API_KEY=name:secret
# OPENSCIENTIST_URL=https://www.openscientist.io
# Verify without submitting a job: just deep-research-canary openscientist

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenAI GPT-Rosalind — `just research-trait <category> <slug> --provider rosalind`
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GPT-Rosalind is a research-preview model gated by OpenAI's trusted-access
# program; TraitMech drives it through deep-research-client's `openai` provider
# with an explicit model id. Prefer the dedicated name: when ROSALIND_API_KEY is
# set it OVERRIDES OPENAI_API_KEY for the rosalind provider, so a general-purpose
# OpenAI key in your shell cannot silently take the call to an org that has no
# access to the model. A bare OPENAI_API_KEY also works if it is the Rosalind key.
# ROSALIND_API_KEY=
#
# Model id requested from the API. Leave unset for the default in
# scripts/research_trait.py; `just rosalind-canary` prints which Rosalind ids the
# credential can actually see, and this is where a snapshot name goes.
# ROSALIND_MODEL=gpt-rosalind

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Alternate names for the SAME credential — normally leave these unset
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EDISON_PLATFORM_API_KEY is what the edison_client SDK reads natively.
# FUTUREHOUSE_API_KEY is a deprecated alias kept for older tooling; the client
# emits a DeprecationWarning when it falls back to it.
#
# Setting either *in addition to* EDISON_API_KEY is the trap: if the two hold
# keys for different Edison accounts, `just research-trait` (which loads .env)
# and `python scripts/research_trait.py` (which does not) authenticate as
# different accounts, and your task history and billing silently split between
# them. Set exactly one credential, here.
#
# EDISON_PLATFORM_API_KEY=
# FUTUREHOUSE_API_KEY=
